  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "QuickTUI for DeepSeek Harness",
      "text": "English | [简体中文](https://github.com/dualface/quicktui-dsh/blob/main/README.zh.md)\n\nSet up [QuickTUI](https://quicktui.ai/) from dsh: install QuickTUI server on this computer, pair the QuickTUI app on your phone, and follow your dsh sessions from it."
    },
    {
      "section": "Set up",
      "text": "1. **QuickTUI server.** The page checks whether QuickTUI server is installed on this computer.\n   - macOS and Linux: select **Install QuickTUI server**. dsh downloads the official install script\n     and runs it with your user account. It installs the latest QuickTUI server release. It is the\n     same as running\n     `curl -fsSL https://quicktui.ai/q.sh | sh -s -- install --channel server2 -y`\n     (in China mainland, `https://dl.quicktui.cn/q.sh`). No administrator password is needed.\n   - Windows: install [QuickTUI from the Microsoft Store](https://apps.microsoft.com/detail/9P1SRCZ4CJ8Z),\n     then open it once from the Start menu. The page finds the server within a minute.\n2. **Pair your phone.** Select **Show pairing QR code** and scan the code with the QuickTUI app. The\n   code can be used once and expires after 15 minutes. The page shows when the phone has paired.\n   dsh sessions have no terminal: in the QuickTUI app, tap the chat icon on the server's card to open\n   the chat list, then open a dsh session there. The page shows a picture of that icon.\n3. **Get the app.** [iPhone and iPad](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/id6761338192) ·\n   [Android (preview)](https://quicktui.ai"
    },
    {
      "section": "Set up",
      "text": "More about QuickTUI: website [quicktui.ai](https://quicktui.ai/) (global) ·\n[quicktui.cn](https://quicktui.cn/) (China mainland); user guide [quicktui.ai/guide](https://quicktui.ai/guide/) ·\n[quicktui.cn/guide](https://quicktui.cn/guide/). The plugin page lists these links too."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh sessions in QuickTUI",
      "text": "With a QuickTUI server version that supports dsh, the plugin connects your dsh sessions to\nQuickTUI. On your phone you can:\n\n- follow each session's status and conversation;\n- answer tool approvals (allow once or reject) and dsh questions;\n- send a prompt, which waits behind the running turn, and interrupt a turn."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh sessions in QuickTUI",
      "text": "A request stays open on the dsh card too: the first answer wins. Subagent work shows inside its\nparent session. To turn the connection off, set `bridge: false` for `quicktui-dsh` in the profile's\n`cordis.patch.yml`.\n\nThe plugin needs the `desktop` or `web` profile."
    }
  ],
